From 18ba975b8406d11097c1b4bc53bb948fe69143ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenCode <twinexotica@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 08:38:17 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] 0230: panel cold restart around the VCI cut (INTF_1 + DSI
 video off/on)

0229 hardware + live /dev/pmem pokes: after a VCI cut or a reset pulse the
K6 DDIC never shows a picture again, whatever we send (whole on-command in
LP or HS). Reads with the stream running never return (RDBK_DATA_CTRL stays
0; the ABL's link-idle reads left 0x29 bytes). Stopping only the DSI video
engine while INTF_1 kept pushing overflowed the DSI FIFO and the stream did
not restart. The DT says qcom,mdss-dsi-lp11-init: Linux and the ABL stop the
timing engine and the video engine, so the lanes sit in LP-11 during the
reset and the on-command goes out in command mode, and start video last.

Sleep: 28/10 (HS) -> INTF_1 timing engine off, 25 ms -> DSI video engine off
(lanes LP-11) -> DCS read 0x0A (expect 0x08) -> reset low -> VCI off.
Wake: VCI on -> reset pulse (link idle) -> clear DSI errors -> on-command
(LP, command mode) -> DCS read 0x0A (expect 0x9c) -> DSI video on -> INTF_1
on. beamWait skipped while the stream is off. Link state logged at each
step ("SWEET PANEL: link (...)"). sweetpanelcold=0 = the 0229 sequence;
bits 2 (soft reset + snapshot restore) and 4 (CTL0 flush) are off here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

